"Reconciles an opening total to a closing total through sequential additive increases and decreases.\n\nUse when: A total changes through named contributions that can be summed. Readers need to see which components explain the net difference.\n\nAvoid when: Changes compound multiplicatively or intermediate steps are not additive.\n\nVisual grammar: Floating bar endpoints encode preceding and following running totals. Bar direction or color encodes positive and negative contributions.\n\nBuild: Start with the opening total anchored at zero. Compute cumulative endpoints for every ordered contribution and draw floating bars. Finish with a zero-based closing total and label contributions directly.\n\nCheck: Verify opening total plus all contributions equals the closing total. Check subtotal bars do not get added a second time. Confirm currency, sign conventions, and accounting period match.\n\nPitfalls: Do not bridge connectors through contribution labels. Arbitrary ordering can suggest a causal sequence that the data does not support.\n\nExample: Reconcile synthetic revenue from 100 to 118: add new sales, subtract churn, and show the final total.\n\nAlternatives: Diverging bar chart, Stacked bar chart, Sankey diagram."
